-- title:
--   Coefficientwise automorphisms stabilise the blow-up centre J and chart B
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements of $K$ integral over the subalgebra generated by $j$ over $A$; $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the scheme obtained as the pushout of the morphisms `fFin`, `fInf` of spectra attached to the $j$-chart and the $j^{-1}$-chart; $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ for the stalk of $X$ at a point $z$, and $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$ for its adic completion with respect to its maximal ideal.
--
--   Arithmetic data. A prime $q$ with $q \ge 5$; a natural number $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero and an element $\xi \in L$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity. The hypothesis `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. An intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries L` is given, and `hK` identifies it with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, $K$ is generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions for $\Gamma_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Coefficient ring. $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, Henselian local and with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \subseteq L \subseteq K$; moreover $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). The element $j \in K$ is nonzero and `hj` states that its Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1} + \dots$ of the modular $j$-function with coefficients transported to $L$. An element $\varpi \in A$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Supersingular point. $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$. A point $z$ of $X$ is given together with the element $\varpi_z$ of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ obtained as the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ which is the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` (`hϖz`), and `hz` requires $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$. A point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C =$ `XFin A ↥K j` is given with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ (`hy'`), the same supersingularity condition `hss'` for ring homomorphisms $C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and `hy'y` asserting $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$.
--
--   Drinfeld chart. $W_1$ is a discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), and $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and
--   $$f_1 - (X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$$
--   (`hf₁`, the right-hand difference being taken against [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)). Finally $e_1$ is a ring isomorphism
--   $$e_1 : \widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\,C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1 - f_1u_1\,\bigr).$$
--   In the clauses below, `toC` is the canonical map $\mathcal O_{X,z} \to \widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$, `mkS` the quotient map $W_1[[X_0,X_1]] \to S$, and `germY` the canonical ring homomorphism $C \to \mathcal O_{X,z}$ obtained from the identification of $C$ with the sections of $\operatorname{Spec} C$, the isomorphism on sections of `ιFin` over $\top$, and the germ at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses, concerning the chart $e_1$ and the automorphisms of $K$ attached to the level structure. Here, for $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ is called a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ when [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) holds, i.e. for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ (with $H$ as above) having integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ with $p_g \ne 0$ in `LaurentSeries ℚ`, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the coefficientwise image $\iota(\tau x)$ multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`. The seven clauses are:
--
--   (i) for every $a \in A$, $e_1$ carries the image in $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$ of the germ at $z$ of the section coming from $a$ via `toBase` to $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1 a))$;
--
--   (ii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$;
--
--   (iii) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$, every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $C$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ for all $a \in C$;
--
--   (iv) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and fixing $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ pointwise modulo $y'$ in the sense of (iii), there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W_1$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W_1)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines the map $C \to S$, $a \mapsto e_1(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_{y'}(a)))$, with the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$; $\theta$ fixes $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))$ for all $w \in W_1$; $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(X_{j}))- \mathrm{mk}_S\bigl(\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\bigr) \in (\mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)^2$ for $j = 0,1$; $c^{q+1} - 1 \in \mathfrak m_{W_1}$; $M_{ij} - c\,\gamma_{ij} \in \mathfrak m_{W_1}$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ then $c - 1 \in \mathfrak m_{W_1}$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak m_{W_1}$;
--
--   (v) for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that each $P_i$ omits at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0$, $\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, each contains $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and each contains an element $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct;
--
--   (vi) for every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_S X_0$, $\mathrm{mk}_S X_1$, containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and containing an element $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a \in C$: the image of $a$ in $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, at every index $n \in \mathbb Z$, lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$;
--
--   (vii) a Drinfeld chart witness: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the series obtained from the $q$-expansion of $j$ by multiplying all exponents by $q\ell$ — lies in $K$ and indeed in $C$; there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference of this element and $a_0$ lying in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that, first, for all $a,b \in W_1$ of which at least one is a unit and with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak m_{W_1}$, the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} (\text{coefficient of } X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i} \text{ in } h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W_1$, and second, $e_1$ carries the image in $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{X,z}$ of the germ of `jqNModC`$-a_0$ to $\mathrm{mk}_S(h)$.
--
--   The centre and the blow-up chart. An ideal $J$ of $C$ is given, and `hJ` states that $J$ is the infimum (intersection) of the set of ideals $J'$ of $C$ for which there exist $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, and $J'$ equal to the contraction along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_{y'}$ of the ideal $\bigl(\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\, \mathrm{mk}_S X_0,\, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1\bigr)$ of $S$. A subalgebra $B$ of $K$ over $A$ is given, and `hB` states that $B$ is, after restriction of scalars to $A$, the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\,\varpi_t = i\}$, i.e. $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every ring automorphism $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ such that
--
--   — $\tau$ acts coefficientwise through $\sigma_L$: for all $x \in K$, the Laurent series of $\tau x$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffMap σL`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) applied to the Laurent series of $x$;
--
--   — $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$ (`hτC`) and $\tau^{-1}$ maps $C$ into $C$ (`hτC'`);
--
--   — there is a unit $w$ of $A$ with $\tau(\varpi_t) = w\varpi_t$ in $K$;
--
--   — there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a ring automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W_1$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $a \mapsto e_1(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_{y'}(a)))$ with the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$; $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(C(w))) = \mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_W w))$ for all $w \in W_1$; $\sigma_W(\sigma_1\varpi_t) = t\,\sigma_1\varpi_t$ for some unit $t \in W_1$; and $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S(X_j)) - \mathrm{mk}_S\bigl(\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\bigr) \in (\mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)^2$ for $j = 0,1$;
--
--   then both of the following hold: first, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ maps $J$ into $J$, that is, $\tau(a) \in J$ for every $a \in J$; and second, $\tau(f) \in B$ for every $f \in B$.
--
--   This is the invariance step for the weighted blow-up used to resolve the integral model of the modular curve at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: an automorphism of $K$ acting coefficientwise on Laurent series (as the inertia action on the coefficient field does) permutes the level automorphisms indexed by $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, hence preserves the intersection $J$ of the local centres and the chart algebra $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. It is invoked in the construction of the Drinfeld fibre of the blown-up chart together with the inertia and decomposition data, and it uses the two conjugation statements [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_apply_conj_of_coeffMap_ringEquiv`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_apply_conj_of_coeffMap_ringEquiv) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_conj_of_isLevelAutAt_of_isPrimitiveRoot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_conj_of_isLevelAutAt_of_isPrimitiveRoot).
